WEBVTT

00:16:29.443 --> 00:16:31.153
So wages can catch up.

00:16:31.153 --> 00:16:34.114
I saw an amazing statistic, actually,
the other day in the UK,

00:16:34.156 --> 00:16:36.908
which showed that a majority
of homeowners in the UK

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:39.828
are happy to have zero growth
on house prices.

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:41.496
And that makes sense.

00:16:41.538 --> 00:16:43.999
Why would you want
your house to gain in value?

00:16:43.999 --> 00:16:45.834
All it means is you buy another house,

00:16:45.834 --> 00:16:49.087
which has relatively gone up as well.

00:16:49.129 --> 00:16:51.673
And I think people acknowledge
that this isn’t working

00:16:51.715 --> 00:16:53.967
for people who rent,
who don't own the assets.

00:16:53.967 --> 00:16:56.636
And I would rather keep that price flat,

00:16:56.636 --> 00:16:59.723
and, you know, have more people
included in our economy.

00:16:59.723 --> 00:17:02.851
But that's, I think,
the big structural challenge --